# scripts/issue_join_code.py writes the plaintext share token here by default,
# and it is a redeemable grant until somebody turns it off.
#
# The glob rather than the one name: a second code was issued on 2026-09-16 (for the
# archived storyboard, so the Past section is not empty for a new visitor) and its file was
# joincode-archived.txt, which this list did not cover. It sat untracked in the repository
# root, one `git add -A` away from being published. Any joincode*.txt is the same thing.
joincode*.txt

# scripts/seed_demo.py --secrets-out defaults to this, and it holds every cast member's
# password alongside the plaintext join code. joincode.txt was listed here from the start
# and this one was missed, which is the more dangerous half of the same pair: a join code
# can be revoked, while a password opens an account from anywhere until it is changed.
demo-secrets.txt

# arduino-cli build output for the share tag
hardware/share-tag/build/
